        {
          "text": "HUANG Fang-t'ai 黃芳泰 (T. 和士), 1647–1690, soldier, native of P'ing-ho, Fukien, was a younger brother of Huang Fang-shih [q. v.]. When his cousin Huang Fang-tu [q. v.], was besieged in Chang-chou, he fought through the lines and raised a relief army in Kwangtung.",
